 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "There are, but on the top of a mountain,\nNot more than the size which we can able\nPoke with our hands; the rest is disappeared\nThe moment it comes down: there remain\nOnly one and two, in the form present\nOf man's attachment to his ideal,\nBut all remain unsought or sought never.\nI have not seen many whom I believe\nWere the great ones that we admire even\nIn the last century. 'Tis vain indeed,\nAs this and other things are completely\nDissected, if we try to compare",
